OL,3,GNEWSADrivers told 'take responsibility'
OL,4,Aas deaths rise
OL,5,
OL,6,FRoad safety campaigners in Lincolnshire
OL,7,Fhave criticised drivers' poor behaviour
OL,8,Fafter the number of people killed in
OL,9,Fcrashes on the county's roads hit a
OL,10,Ffive-year high.
OL,12,FBetween 1 January and 31 October, 44
OL,13,Ffatalities were recorded, up from 26
OL,14,Fthe year before, according to the
OL,15,FLincolnshire Road Safety Partnership.
OL,17,FSpokesman Simon Outen-Coe said: "Too
OL,18,Foften, drivers blame the roads or other
OL,19,Fpeople and treat speed limits as though
OL,20,Fthey're optional.
OL,23,APub: 03-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
